{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/will-and-preferences",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "will and preferences"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "The standard that must guide the exercise of legal capacity and any support in decision-making: what the person wants and prefers, not what others consider objectively best for them."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "The CRPD, as interpreted by General Comment No. 1 (2014), replaces the \"best interests\" model as applied to adults with respect for their will and preferences. Where, after serious efforts, these cannot be determined, the best interpretation of the person's will and preferences must apply, never a substitute decision. It is a central standard against paternalism, substitute guardianship and infantilisation."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "10.4.2"
  ],
